      "content": "Targeted programs can be more efficient and cost-effective, as they focus resources on specific populations that are most in need, reducing waste and minimizing systemic risks. However, this benefit must be balanced against the fact that unmet needs of vulnerable communities can have long-term social consequences, such as increased inequality and diminished social cohesion, ultimately undermining economic stability. Targeted programs can create a vicious cycle of dependency and stigma, whereas UBI has the potential to promote social cohesion and overall welfare.",
